<title>UK: Turkey sets $250 mln five-year bond, 350 b.p. over.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets $250 mln five-year bond, 350 b.p. over.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers J.P. Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TURKEY</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     10.00     MATURITY    23.MAY.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    23.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+350 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  B	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	HOME CTRY  TURKEY    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 30.APR.02</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
